This file removes the need for a code change. The loader already supports regional secrets, and setting one environment variable turns it on. Before I write commands, I'll check the exact gcloud syntax for regional secrets.## What the file shows

- **Setting `SECRET_LOCATION=me-central2` switches the app to regional secrets.** The loader then builds the path `projects/<project>/locations/me-central2/secrets/CN_STAGING_<KEY>/versions/latest` and calls the `me-central2-secretmanager.googleapis.com` endpoint. With no value set, it uses the global secrets, which is today's behavior. That means no code change, only an environment variable, with one caveat below.
- **It reads only 18 of your 23 secrets.** These are `DB_HOST`, `DB_USERNAME`, `DB_PASSWORD`, `DB_DATABASE`, `DB_PORT`, `GCP_BUCKET`, `GCP_FILE_PATH`, `MAIL_DRIVER`, `MAIL_HOST`, `MAIL_PORT`, `MAIL_USERNAME`, `MAIL_PASSWORD`, `MAIL_FROM_NAME`, `MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS`, `REDIS_HOST`, `REDIS_PORT`, `REDIS_PASSWORD` and `EMAIL_SENDING_ENABLED`. The other five (`BASE_URL`, `FRONTEND_URL`, `MAIL_ENCRYPTION`, `SOCKET_URL`, `SUB_DOMAIN_URL`) aren't read by this build, so I can't tell whether anything else uses them.

⚠️ **The caveat:** this code uses the older endpoint form. Google's current docs show the REST address as `secretmanager.LOCATION.rep.googleapis.com`. I haven't verified that the older host still works for `me-central2`, so step 1 tests both. If only the new form works, the loader needs a one-line change.

The steps use scripts, not the Console, because the Console would put 18 secret values on your screen. Nothing below prints a value.

## Step 1: test with one low-risk secret

Run this on the backend instance you're logged into:
```bash
P=pg-ae-n-app-125609; L=me-central2
gcloud secrets create CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER --location=$L --project=$P
gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER --project=$P | gcloud secrets versions add CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER --location=$L --project=$P --data-file=-
gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER --project=$P | sha256sum
gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER --location=$L --project=$P | sha256sum
```
The two hashes must be identical, which shows the same bytes without revealing them. The docs show `--location` and `--data-file=-` for regional secrets, but also say Secret Manager must be set up to use a regional endpoint. If gcloud complains about that, paste the error.

**Test both endpoint forms.** The output is discarded, so no value is printed:
```bash
T=$(gcloud auth print-access-token)
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "older host: %{http_code}\n" -H "Authorization: Bearer $T" "https://me-central2-secretmanager.googleapis.com/v1/projects/$P/locations/$L/secrets/CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER/versions/latest:access"
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "rep host: %{http_code}\n" -H "Authorization: Bearer $T" "https://secretmanager.$L.rep.googleapis.com/v1/projects/$P/locations/$L/secrets/CN_STAGING_MAIL_DRIVER/versions/latest:access"
```
- **`older host` returns 200:** no code change needed.
- **Only `rep host` returns 200:** the loader needs a one-line change.

